  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "freerdp security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for freerdp is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "FreeRDP is a client implementation of the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) that follows Microsoft\u0026apos;s open specifications. This package provides the client applications xfreerdp.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nFreeRDP is a free implementation of the Remote Desktop Protocol. Prior to 3.27.0, FreeRDP clients using TS Gateway accept a server-controlled max_xmit_frag value in libfreerdp/core/gateway/rpc_bind.c without bounding it to the 4088-byte ReceiveFragment allocation. A malicious gateway can advertise 65535 and then send a response fragment of the same length, causing rpc_channel_read in libfreerdp/core/gateway/rpc.c to write up to 65535 bytes into the smaller ReceiveFragment buffer. This can crash the client and may permit code execution through attacker-controlled heap corruption. This issue is fixed in version 3.27.0.(CVE-2026-55193)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for freerdp is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of high. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "High",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "freerdp",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
